Z||000000||shiloh187||03-23-2001||05:43 PM||||I bought a used 87 Iron Duke.  I have it at the mechanics now and he put a new manifold on it.  He says now though that with the new manifold and o2 sensor it still runs like crap.  <P>Basically it will stay on as long as you are giving it gas, but it wont idle on its own.  So if you let go of the gas pedal, it dies out on me.  Also, it has no pickup.  He is going to try a few things he said and will let me know.<P>Anyone have any ideas?  And if it is too drastic to fix, how much is a new engine gonna cost me to drop into it?<P>thanx<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||03-23-2001||06:01 PM||||It doesn't sound like the engine needs to be replaced, unless it rattles...<BR>Check the obvious, vacuume leaks, EGR leak, inop IAC valve, MAP sensor,PVC valve, etc...<BR>It takes time and patience to diagnose these tron engines, not like the bad old days of carbs and points...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-23-2001||07:55 PM||||Any of a number of things. All of which a decent mechanic should be able to find quickly. DIS motors are not dificult to work on. Non idle is most likely a vac leak or a bad IAC or some jackass fooled with the TBI idle stop. No pickup also points to vac problems, and posibly the MAP is bad or has a vac line problem. <P>The exhaust manifolds on 87-88, and properly recalled 84-86, 4 cyls get broken fairly easy. 1 cause is water dumped on them when they are hot. The deck lid unloads right onto them.<P>||||reg||1
